1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
Okay chapter number one why you're getting journaling wrong.
好，第一章：为什么你的写日记方式可能有问题。

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:09,321
Not enough people talk about this they're always throwing extra ideas on how we can journal and I personally think it's confusing.
谈这个问题的人不够多；大家不断抛出更多写日记的想法，我个人觉得让人困惑。

3
00:00:09,321 --> 00:00:11,360
It's overwhelming you never know where to start.
信息太多让人不知所措，你不知道从何开始。

4
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:19,321
And you're not actually adapting the journey and the process of journaling to your unique needs and your personal life which is essential.
而且你没有把写日记的过程调整到符合自己的独特需求和个人生活，这一点很关键。

5
00:00:19,321 --> 00:00:26,761
I also think a lot of brands and a lot of people had normalized this process of journaling in 5 minutes or only writing three lines a day.
我也觉得许多品牌和许多人让“五分钟写日记”或“每天只写三行”成为常态。

6
00:00:26,761 --> 00:00:30,440
Which I can definitely see is great for a beginner or getting started.
我当然理解，这对新手或刚开始的人可能很好。

7
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:40,160
But at the end of the day journaling is about writing as much as you can to actually start to understand and analyze and process and learn from the thoughts you have going in your mind.
但说到底，我认为写日记是尽量写出来，以开始理解、分析、处理自己的念头，并从中学习。

8
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:46,720
I'm talking deep in the back of your mind all the way in your subconscious the thoughts that you're not even consciously aware of day today.
我说的是脑海深处、潜意识中的念头，那些你平日甚至没意识到的想法。

9
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:51,241
When you take the time to jud and write one full page or a double page spread.
当你花时间写满一页，或写满展开的两页时，

10
00:00:51,241 --> 00:00:55,471
That's when you are really going to make progress you are really going to build that connection with yourself.
作者认为，这样才会取得进展，并建立与自己的连接。

11
00:00:55,481 --> 00:01:02,321
Writing three lines about I'm grateful for this I ate this this is how much water I drank is it making real change on your journey.
只写三行“我感激这个、吃了这个、喝了多少水”，真的让你的成长过程发生变化了吗？

12
00:01:02,321 --> 00:01:06,601
It's an example of aesthetic self development without any real substance behind it.
作者把这称作好看却没有实际内容支撑的自我提升。

13
00:01:06,601 --> 00:01:15,641
But to really dive into why we get journaling wrong and what that looks like so you really get it I'm going to bring in our favorite girls to illustrate this example.
为了深入解释为什么写日记可能没达到预期、具体是什么样，我要请出我们熟悉的两个女孩来举例。

14
00:01:15,641 --> 00:01:22,991
Lola and athena both of these gires are on their self development journeys they both want to level up into the best version of themselves in 2025.
Lola 和 Athena 都在自我提升，都想在2025年成为更好的自己。

15
00:01:23,001 --> 00:01:28,801
And they've been journaling for a while because g it's literally everybody's wellness routines why would they not.
她们已经写了一阵日记，因为这几乎是每个人的养生习惯之一，为什么不写呢？

16
00:01:28,801 --> 00:01:33,001
But they do journal slightly differently and this is how they do it.
但她们写法稍有不同，下面看看她们怎么做。

17
00:01:33,001 --> 00:01:38,871
I try to be really consistent with my journaling I just open it up every single day and just write whatever comes to my mind.
第一种说法：我尽量坚持写日记，每天打开，想到什么就写什么。

18
00:01:38,881 --> 00:01:44,001
Whenever I open up my journal and I'm about to write first I take a moment to actually set an intention.
另一种说法：每次打开日记准备写之前，我会先花一点时间确定意图。

19
00:01:44,001 --> 00:01:48,151
This helps me gain clarity on what I actually want to explore today and get to the rout of.
这样能让我弄清今天想探索什么、想深入了解什么。

20
00:01:48,161 --> 00:01:51,721
Maybe sometimes it's because I have some emotional stuff I need to get off my chest.
也许有时是因为我有些情绪想倾诉出来。

21
00:01:51,721 --> 00:01:54,921
Maybe sometimes it's because I need clarity on goals that I'm thinking about.
也许有时是因为，我需要理清正在考虑的目标。

22
00:01:54,921 --> 00:01:59,561
It's honestly just all suited to me and my personal needs so that I can make real progress on my journey.
总之，我会按自己和个人需求来安排，好让自己真正有所进展。

23
00:01:59,561 --> 00:02:06,881
What do I write in my journal um just about my day like I just write my thoughts and just document what I'm thinking.
“我在日记里写什么？就是一天的事，写想法，记录自己在想什么。”

24
00:02:06,881 --> 00:02:10,361
Oh I really died deep into my thoughts and feelings.
“我会深入自己的想法和感受。”原字幕 died deep 待复核。

25
00:02:10,361 --> 00:02:15,601
Sometimes it's not even about documenting my entire day but really fixating on something that stood out to me that day.
有时不必记一整天，而是特别关注当天某件引起我注意的事。

26
00:02:15,601 --> 00:02:20,721
So that I can fully process it and I'm not bringing old baggage into the rest of the week.
这样我才能充分处理它，不把旧的情绪包袱带进本周剩下的日子。

27
00:02:20,721 --> 00:02:25,041
Oh yeah I f up so many pages in my journal this is like my third journal now.
“我写满好多页了，这好像已经是我的第三本日记。”f up 原词不明，待听辨。

28
00:02:25,041 --> 00:02:28,400
I just keep writing and writing and storing up all of my journals.
“我一直写、一直写，把所有日记本都存起来。”

29
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:34,001
I don't think there's any point in journaling and filling up those of journals if you're not actually going to go back and read through them.
“我觉得，如果不回头读，光写日记、写满许多本并没有意义。”

30
00:02:34,001 --> 00:02:39,400
Because that is where you're going to find all of your patterns and all of the gold and the answers to your problems.
因为回看时，才能发现自己的模式、宝贵之处，以及问题的答案。

31
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:47,471
So I make it a habit every month or sometimes every week I have alerts in my calendar to remind me to go back through my journal and read through my old entries.
所以我每月、有时每周会固定回看，设日历提醒，重读以前的记录。

32
00:02:47,481 --> 00:02:52,321
It really helps me see how I've grown so that I can feel proud of myself and celebrate my successes.
这能帮我看见成长，为自己骄傲，并庆祝已有的成功。

33
00:02:52,321 --> 00:02:57,520
But also what I need to work on if there are any cycles that I can clearly read that I am still stuck in.
也能看出还需要改进什么，是否还陷在某些反复出现的循环里。

34
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:03,790
I think it's so good to journal whenever you feel upset or you're going through something negative I love that.
“我觉得难过或经历负面事件时写日记很好，我很喜欢。”

35
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:13,110
Like I will literally open up my journal and I will scribble everything out and I will just vent and vent and get all of my complaints off my test is the best.
“我会打开日记，把一切草草写出来，不断倾诉，把抱怨全倒出来，太好了。”test 等字幕待核。

36
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:19,041
Sometimes I love using pages to just vent and get all of my emotions onto papers so then afterwards I can think about them more clearly.
“有时我也爱用纸页倾诉，把情绪写下来，随后可以更清楚地思考。”

37
00:03:19,041 --> 00:03:20,120
But I don't just vent.
但我不会只停留在倾诉上。

38
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:27,201
Once I've got all of that thought and emotion onto paper I start to think about how I can start dealing with that in a healthy way and how I want to move forward.
把想法和情绪写下来后，我会开始思考怎样妥善处理、下一步怎样往前走。
